Rama eyes humble Sita and begins with inward anger --- Rama declares foe conquered manliness done wrath ended insult wiped --- Rama says labour fruitful vow crossed and Hanuman leap Sugriva host Vibhishana devotion fruitful --- Tear-eyed Sita hears like frightened doe --- Rama anger flares like ghee-fed fire frowns sidelong and speaks harsh among monkeys rakshasas --- Rama says he freed her from indignation not for her but by friends prowess to guard conduct and lineage slur --- Rama calls doubted Sita facing him displeasing like lamp to sore eyes --- Rama permits her to go ten directions needing her not and choose Lakshmana Bharata Sugriva or Vibhishana --- Rama says nobleman cannot take Ravana-eyed wife proclaiming great lineage and won fame without attachment --- Rama says Ravana could not forbear lovely Sita in his house --- Mithili trembles sheds tears like creeper struck by elephant trunk hearing unwelcome beloved words